Show runs with wild
sig render : [wild] (() -> String) fun render() { show(42) } render()
stdout : "42" : String

Show requires wild even for an integer
sig render : [] (() -> String) fun render() { show(42) } render()
stderr : @.*Type error: The modalities require different effect contexts.*
exit : 1

Date parsing runs with wild
sig parse : [wild] ((String) -> DateTime) fun parse(s) { parseDate(s) } parse("1970-01-01 00:00:00+0") == intToDate(0)
stdout : true : Bool

Date parsing requires wild even with an explicit offset
sig parse : [] (() -> DateTime) fun parse() { parseDate("1970-01-01 00:00:00+0") } parse()
stderr : @.*Type error: The modalities require different effect contexts.*
exit : 1

Sleep reaches its runtime error with wild
sig wait : [wild] (() -> ()) fun wait() { sleep(1) } wait()
stderr : @.*Runtime error: The sleep function is not implemented on the server yet.*
exit : 1

Sleep requires wild
sig wait : [] (() -> ()) fun wait() { sleep(1) } wait()
stderr : @.*Type error: The modalities require different effect contexts.*
exit : 1

Error can raise in an empty effect context
sig fail : [] (() -> Int) fun fail() { error("pure failure") } fail()
stderr : @.*Runtime error: pure failure.*
exit : 1

Exit ends evaluation with its argument
sig stop : [wild] (() -> Int) fun stop() { exit(42); 0 } stop()
stdout : 42 : Int

Exit requires wild
sig stop : [] (() -> Int) fun stop() { exit(42) } stop()
stderr : @.*Type error: The modalities require different effect contexts.*
exit : 1

Exit accepts an absolute function and has a separate result type at each call
(if (false) exit(()) else true, if (false) exit(fun() { 42 } : [] (() -> Int)) else 42)
stdout : (true, 42) : (Bool, Int)

Exit rejects an ambient function argument
exit(fun() { 42 })
stderr : @.*Type error: Type argument .* must satisfy Abs.*
exit : 1

Exit rejects an absolute linear argument
exit(linfun() { 42 } : [] (() -@ Int))
stderr : @.*Type error: Type argument .* must satisfy Unl.*
exit : 1

Exit rejects a linear result type argument
(~exit)[Int, [] (() -@ Int)]
stderr : @.*Type error: Type argument .* must satisfy Unl.*
exit : 1
